{"_v":1,"id":"a-man-for-all-seasons-2008","bd":{"positive":5,"mixed":1,"negative":3},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2008/10/08/theater/reviews/08brantley.html","d":"2008-10-19","q":"Surely, it would be more rewarding than being the fixed if towering center of a shrine."},{"cn":"David Rooney","o":"Variety","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.variety.com/review/VE1117938631.html?categoryid=33&amp;cs=1","d":"2014-04-22","q":"The Roundabout staging becomes more gripping as it proceeds, driven by a performance from Frank Langella as measured and naturalistic as it is majestic."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Associated Press","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://hosted.ap.org/dynamic/stories/T/THEATER_REVIEW_SEASONS_GENT-?SITE=WVTMTV&amp;SECTION=ENTERTAINMENT&amp;TEMPLATE=DEFAULT","d":"2014-04-22","q":"With a strong, even mesmerizing physical presence, Langella slips easily into costume drama."},{"cn":"Elysa Gardner","o":"USA Today","s":75,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.usatoday.com/life/theater/reviews/2008-10-07-man-for-all-seasons_N.htm","d":"2014-04-22","q":"It seems as good a time as any for the Roundabout Theatre Company to revive A Man for All Seasons."},{"cn":"David Finkle","o":"TheaterMania","s":70,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.theatermania.com/new-york-city-theater/reviews/a-man-for-all-seasons_13058.html","d":"2008-03-14","q":"Langella brings both gravitas and humanity to the role."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":45,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/ManAllSeasons.html","d":"2014-04-22","q":"If the star in question is Frank Langella, the answer is almost."},{"cn":"Jeremy Gerard","o":"New York Post","s":44,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"https://nypost.com/2008/10/18/seasons-of-woe/","d":"2008-10-18","q":"Frank Langella brings his customary gravity and intelligence to the role of Thomas More, but even his commanding presence can't save this leaden revival."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"amNewYork","s":42,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"http://www.amny.com/entertainment/am-man1008,0,7431943.story","d":"2014-04-22","q":"But to be frank, Doug Hughes' straightforward production is as dull and lifeless as it is altogether unnecessary."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/a-man-for-all-seasons/","d":"2008-10-15","q":"That Langella renders the role so humanly that we can identify with him is the reason to see this revival at Theatre."}],"au":{"score":82,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"ss":{"s":86,"c":7},"mz":{"s":70,"c":2,"sr":3.5}}},"hi":"/images/shows/a-man-for-all-seasons-2008/hero.webp","ta":"227 W 42nd St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2008-09-12","ca":[{"n":"Frank Langella","r":"Sir Thomas More"},{"n":"Charles Borland","r":"The Jailor"},{"n":"Curt Bouril","r":"Attendant"},{"n":"Peter Bradbury","r":"Matthew"},{"n":"Hannah Cabell","r":"Margaret More"},{"n":"Alex Cole","r":"Attendant"},{"n":"Emily Dorsch","r":"Barmaid"},{"n":"Michael Esper","r":"William Roper"},{"n":"Elizabeth Gilbert","r":"Attendant"},{"n":"Michel Gill","r":"The Duke of Norfolk"},{"n":"Miguel Govea","r":"Attendant"},{"n":"Zach Grenier","r":"Thomas Cromwell"},{"n":"Einar Gunn","r":"Attendant"},{"n":"Patricia Hodges","r":"Catherine Anger"},{"n":"Andy Lutz","r":"Attendant"},{"n":"Dakin Matthews","r":"Cardinal Wolsey"},{"n":"George Morfogen","r":"Thomas Cranmer"},{"n":"Patrick Page","r":"King Henry VIII"},{"n":"Maryann Plunkett","r":"Alice More"},{"n":"Triney Sandoval","r":"Signor Chapuys"},{"n":"Jeremy Strong","r":"Richard Rich"}]}